{"id": 32, "ts": 1780463181.5907106, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I agree with Emily that Candidate\u202fB remains the strongest overall, but I want to highlight a new comparative point: Candidate\u202fC, while described as \u201c100\u202f% reliable\u201d and able to \u201ccreate a positive atmosphere with his crew,\u201d also \u201chas difficulty communicating ideas\u201d and is \u201cregarded as egocentric.\u201d Those communication weaknesses directly affect crew cooperation and professional communication\u2014key safety\u2011critical criteria. In contrast, Candidate\u202fB\u2019s communication issues are limited to \u201cpretentious\u201d tone and occasional \u201cnasty remarks,\u201d which, although concerning, are less likely to impair day\u2011to\u2011day cockpit coordination than a candidate who struggles to convey ideas at all. Given that we have no evidence of B\u2019s communication causing operational risk, and C\u2019s communication deficits are more fundamental, I maintain my provisional recommendation for Candidate\u202fB."}
